WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.920
Orion PM. Get excited about it, it's

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:03.200
a lot of fun, I'm here to

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:04.460
show you what we're doing. Watch what

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:05.900
happens when I make them claim it

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:08.380
first. One gets the job and the

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:10.433
other gets told to stop.

00:00:10.433 --> 00:00:14.293
First, I probe the work that

00:00:14.293 --> 00:00:16.407
overlaps. If you find a live holder,

00:00:16.927 --> 00:00:19.023
stop and coordinate with that worker. But

00:00:19.023 --> 00:00:20.763
I still have to claim the task

00:00:20.763 --> 00:00:23.703
because another worker can arrive after I

00:00:23.703 --> 00:00:27.123
read the probe result, right? You understand

00:00:27.123 --> 00:00:28.523
what I'm saying? So I've got two

00:00:28.523 --> 00:00:31.863
separate command line processes waiting at the

00:00:31.863 --> 00:00:34.443
same starting point. I let both of

00:00:34.443 --> 00:00:36.867
them ask for this one task and

00:00:37.163 --> 00:00:39.643
there's the result one process returned to

00:00:39.643 --> 00:00:42.243
zero and got a live claim and

00:00:42.243 --> 00:00:45.133
the other returned three and was refused
